 "posts": [
  {
   "slug": "the-00-52-last-train",
   "title": "The 00:52 last train",
   "date": "2026-11-12",
   "categories": [
    "night-desk"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "last-train",
    "standard-pod"
   ],
   "image": "assets/images/demo/p18-morning-pod.webp",
   "excerpt": "A commuter missing the final connection walks across from the platform to find an open desk, a Standard Pod and a proper sleep before dawn.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The last regional train was due in at 00:52. Ana had a connecting bus that stopped running at midnight and a phone at nine per cent. She crossed Platform Lane with her bag on one shoulder and found the lobby lit and the desk staffed.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Jonah, the night clerk, took her ID, handed over a brass key and pointed to a locker for the bag. A Standard Pod costs €42 for the night and includes a towel set, so there was nothing else to decide at that hour.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>She was in her pod by 01:10 with the curtain closed and the reading light on. Quiet hours run from 22:00 to 07:00, and the corridor stayed silent until the first alarms at six. Check-out is at 10:00, and the East Exit is eighty metres away.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->"
  }
 ],
